(with the matching brace added before case 2's trailing `break;`).
Both folded away before codegen: MWCC canonicalises guard POLARITY and if/else-vs-early-exit nesting into one internal form here.

THE THIRD NAMED FORM IS STRUCTURALLY EXCLUDED, NOT UNTRIED. v1 also proposed `break` out of the for with the k-test moved after the loop. The target's own layout refutes it: at 0x32c the target's `b ->348` jumps PAST `li r25,-1` at 0x344, i.e. the found path skips the k=-1 assignment. A `break` lands ON the loop exit (0x344), so no break-based spelling can reproduce the target's block order. Recorded as excluded-by-target-layout rather than spent as a probe.
